# Keep the build context small and keep host-only artifacts out of the image.
#
# The durable data directory is the big one: it holds the WAL, the bus id, the
# dirlock and (once DUR-12 lands) the MAC key -- none of that belongs baked
# into an image layer, and it is excluded from git for the same reason (see
# .gitignore).
/data/
*.wal
*.log

# Local build output / scratch -- rebuilt inside the image by the builder
# stage, never copied in from the host.
/agent-bus
/bin/
*.test

# VCS and editor/agent metadata -- irrelevant to the build and often large.
.git/
.claude/
.claude/settings.local.json

# Docs and Spec Server bookkeeping -- large, churn frequently, never needed to
# build or run the binary. Keeping them out of the context keeps `docker
# build`'s context-upload step fast.
*.md
!README.md
